Summary

- A computer is an electronic device that processes data into information.
- It follows the IPO (Input, Process, Output) cycle.
- Main characteristics are speed, accuracy, storage, automation, diligence, reliability, and versatility.
- Computers are used in education, banking, hospitals, business, communication, entertainment, and research.
- The four basic parts of a computer are Input Unit, CPU, Memory Unit, and Output Unit.